G230 -- THE dM/dg MEASUREMENT: the acceleration distribution of the dark sector
        dM/dg = (dM_dark/dr)/(dg/dr) per ring; deep index vs -2; Lomax shape vs 2(1+u)^-3
==============================================================================================

--- (1a) SPARC: the differential observable from the G071 committed sample ---
    G071 committed sample: 35 galaxies, 641 rings (G071_results.json)
    shells built: 361  (dropped 245: 117 with dM_dark <= 0 [inner, baryon-dominated], 128 with dg <= 0)
    g/a0: min 0.0741, median 0.393, max 7.90;  dM/dg span log10 16.04 .. 23.27 [Msun/(m s^-2)]
    deep shells (g < 0.3 a0): 126  (35%),  shell dark mass share of the deep window 30%
    galaxies with >= 1 shell: 35; median shells/galaxy 7

--- (1b) HI dwarfs: dark mass at the last measured point (G114) ---
    G114 committed: 55 dwarfs (26 LITTLE THINGS + 29 FIGGS); 26 carry committed g_N/a0 at R_max -> mass elements (29 FIGGS excluded: no committed radius/R_max in this lane's artifacts -- flagged)
    g/a0: min 0.0365, median 0.160, max 3.12;  M_dark: 8.58e+06 .. 7.04e+09 Msun (median 1.04e+09)
    deep elements (g < 0.3 a0): 18/26 (median g_N/a0 of the G114 LT sample: 0.16 -- the deep regime is its home)

--- (1c) MIGHTEE: g_obs values (no committed radii -> no masses) ---
    80 rings, g_obs/a0: min 0.1054, median 0.313, max 1.71;  deep: 37
    NOTE: the committed MIGHTEE artifact carries (g_bar, g_obs) only -- no per-ring radius -> no masses -> enters the distribution tests under an EXPLICIT equal-mass-per-ring assumption (shape-only).

